    "notes": "Four sessions at Columbia 30th Street: Oct 31 1962 (Bye-Ya, Bolivar Blues), Nov 1 (Body and Soul, Bright Mississippi), Nov 2 (Sweet and Lovely, Just a Gigolo, Monk's Dream), Nov 6 (Five Spot Blues). Engineer not credited in any source consulted \u2014 explicit null. Album recorded Oct-Nov 1962, released January 1963 (year recorded as release year; AllMusic lists release year 1962). 'Bright Mississippi' is the only composition Monk had not previously recorded. 2002-reissue alternate takes excluded."
